Add Payment Tracking, payment terms/auto-hold and Invoice History (v0.101)

Payment Tracking:
- New Invoicing > Payment Tracking page, replacing the per-order Payments
  box on Sales Activity. Lists every invoiced order with an outstanding
  balance - company, invoice number, date, order number(s), total, paid,
  outstanding, days since invoiced and days over payment terms. Searchable
  and filterable (close to payment terms / over payment terms / part
  payment), shaded orange near terms and red once over.
- Recording a payment (amount/reference/notes) or applying a company's
  credit balance to an invoice attempts to push full payment to Shopify
  via the GraphQL orderMarkAsPaid mutation for a single-order invoice.
  A consolidated (multi-order) invoice, or a partial payment, is recorded
  here but reported back as "not pushed" with the reason - this app's
  Shopify integration is deliberately GraphQL-only, and there's no
  reliable GraphQL equivalent for an arbitrary partial payment, so nothing
  is guessed at.
- Any amount paid or applied beyond what's owing on the invoice (an
  overpayment) is added to the company's credit balance automatically.
- Payment moved from being linked only to an Order to (going forward)
  being linked to an Invoice, since a consolidated invoice can span
  multiple orders. Order stays populated for legacy traceability.

Payment terms, auto-hold and chasers:
- Company gains a Payment Terms (days) override (falls back to a new
  Settings > Payment Tracking default, 30 days) and an Auto-hold when
  overdue toggle.
- With auto-hold on, a daily job puts a company on hold the first time one
  of its invoices goes over terms, and takes it back off once nothing's
  outstanding - edge-triggered (Invoice.autoHoldTriggered/Company.autoHeld)
  so it never re-holds a company for invoices staff have already decided
  to leave overdue after taking them off hold by hand.
- The same daily job sends two chaser emails per invoice, each only once:
  a warning before terms and an overdue notice on the day. Both templates
  are editable under the new Settings > Payment Tracking section and
  always go to the company's Invoice Email.

RMA credit auto-apply:
- Generating a credit note for an RMA now auto-applies it to the
  outstanding invoice(s) for that RMA's replacement order when one
  already exists, falling back to the company's general credit balance
  (with a warning) when it doesn't.

Invoice History:
- New Invoicing > Invoice History page listing every invoice/credit note
  ever generated, with the same search bar style as the rest of the app.

Sales Activity:
- Shipping cost/courier/service now stays visible after an order is
  released for despatch instead of disappearing.
- Removed the per-order Payments box (superseded by Payment Tracking).

Credit calculation:
- CompanyService.creditUsed() rewritten to a three-bucket model (orders
  not yet despatched, despatched-but-not-invoiced lines, unpaid invoices)
  so nothing is double-counted or falls through a gap now that Payment
  Tracking payments are invoice-linked rather than order-linked.

Also: documented that the password reset link issue reported this release
was a missing Settings > Email > Public URL value, not a code bug (no
code change).

Written and reviewed without a working compiler in this environment
(Maven Central/npm registry both blocked here) - please build and
smoke-test before relying on this, particularly Payment Tracking and the
daily chaser/auto-hold job.

